"stanza2"
"$n sings in a merry voice:
@I 'Twas down at the Crossroads I first went astray...
@I There I drank enough drink 'fore to fill Narak Bay!
@I Goin' up to the mournin' I wore out me shoes
@I Goin' up to the cross for the best of good booze!
"
E
"stanza1"
"$n sings in a merry voice:
@I At the pub on the crossroads there's whisky and beer
@I There's brandy from cognac that's fragrant but dear
@I But for killin' the thirst and for raisin' the gout
@I There's nothin' at all beats a pint of good stout!
"
E
"stanza3"
"$n sings in a merry voice:
@I Some folk o'er the water think bitter is fine
@I And others they swear by the juice of the wine
@I But there's nothin' that's squeezed from the grape or the hop
@I Like the black liquidation with the froth on the top!
"
E
"stanza4"
"$n sings in a merry voice:
@I I've travelled in sandals, I've travelled in pants
@I At the sound of good music I'll sing or I'll dance
@I So hear me then mister and pour me one more
@I If I cannot drink it up then throw me out the door!
"
E
"stanza5"
"$n sings in a merry voice:
@I It's Kha-Da's porter that has me this way
@I For it's sweeter than buttermilk and stronger than tea
@I But when in the mornin' I feel kind of rough
@I I curse the Lord Iveagh who brews the damned stuff!
"
E
"end"
"With a flourish, $n bows and awaits your applause.
"
