claws giving it no appendages with which to grasp objects.  A large,
beetle-like shell covers its torso, and sharp, bony protrusions run up and
down the edges of its carapace-like body.  The final, contradictory
characteristic is the beaked, vulture-like head from which peer two small,
beady eyes.
