"essence"
"The wizened old elf replies, \"Ah, it has been a while but I remember well how
to make the essence of a nightstone.  First you must crush a nightstone in a
mortar and pestle of pure krynite.  That is the only substance that will
maintain the essence of the magic without ruining it.  Then mix in the berries
of an athelas plant for the magical properties contained in it.  Finally, you
must pour the contents into an empty glass vial before the crushed krynite and
athelas berries have a chance to destroy the pestle.  The pestle will still be
ruined but you'll have an elixir containing the essence of a nightstone.\"
"
E
"use"
"The wizened old elf pauses to consider for a moment then adds, \"I haven't
found many uses that I think you'd be interested in for such an elixir but I
remember a fellow a while back who came through asking if he could use it to
imbue some kind of jerkin with magical properties.  It would be a rather
inefficient use for such an elixir but if you poured it over a jerkin of the
right material it might have some beneficial effect.  The fellow never told me
if it worked so I can't help with that.  Good luck.\"
