#1329
""
""
"living wall"
""
""
"blocks the eastern passageway."
"[BUG, BUG, BUG]"
""
""
"- Report to an immortal at once!"
"An amalgam of humanoid body parts, sheathed in sickly pink flesh, this horrid
creation of dark magic has only one purpose: to absorb the life of those who
come within its range, adding their body to its already grotesque collection.
The wall is not composed of whole bodies in their original humanoid form, but
instead many separate parts from many separate humanoid creatures.  Trollish
eyes, an ogrish tuft of hair, skeletal humanoid claws, and drooling open maws
are placed haphazardly on the carpet of flesh.  Non-organic material from the
victims of the wall has dropped to the ground in a heap in front of the wall -
discarded shields, swords, and other articles resistant to the decay-prone
cavern atmosphere.
"
"Nereus"
""
"Nereus"
"i = 1d10+8;
j = 0;
loop( j < i ) {
  rch = rand_player( room );
  if( attack( mob, rch, 5d4+16, \"skeletal clawing\" ) && 1d8 == 5 ) {
    k = find_stat( rch, con );
    if( k == 3 ) {
      act_tochar( #succumb, rch );
      act_notchar( #collapse, rch );
      loop( rch )
        inflict( rch, mob, 999, \"\" );
      }
    if( k <= 7 )
      act_tochar( #danger, rch );
    drain_stat( rch, con, 10, -1 );
    }
  j = j + 1;
  }
i = 10000;
j = 4510;
loop( j < 4514 ) {
  if( obj_in_room( j, room ) )
    i = i / 7;
  j = j + 1;
  }
act_notchar( #wounds, mob );
heal( mob, i );
"
E
"wounds"
"@cThe wounds of $n begin to close, healing before your eyes.@n
"
E
"danger"
"@RYou feel as if your body will soon succumb to the draining attacks.@n
"
E
"succumb"
"@RYour body gives way, your remaining life force tearing away to join the
enormity of the living wall.@n
"
E
"collapse"
"@R$n collapses to the ground, $s remaining life force draining away.@n
"
