"At first glance, the male which stands before you looks like a simple
lizardman, trying to peddle his wares.  His scales, though, are much too dark
and his hands too clawed.  Also, his black tail is thicker than a lizardman's
tail usually is.  Though he covers most of his body in satiny tan, orange, and
yellow scarves, he fails to hide his more serpentine heritage.  Most of his
face is hidden behind scarves, though his lidless, slitted yellow pupils seem
wary.
"
"Florian"
