""
"familiar"
"black dragon"
""
""
"stands here, a malevolent gleam in his eye."
"black dragons"
""
""
"are here."
"Sleek and black as night, this ebony dragon is a juvenile roughly the size of
a horse.  As long again as its body, the dragon's flexible, black tail is
jaggedly tipped with spines and a sharp barb at the end.  The dragon's head is
topped with a double pair of horns that jut out from the sides and curl
slightly inwards, parallelling the sinuous neck.  Sharp, bright white teeth
and razor-sharp burnished black claws make it clear that this creature is well
capable of defending itself.  A malevolent gleam of intelligence is in his
eyes, as if this period of his life is merely a phase that he will soon
outgrow.
"
"Florian"
""
"Talis"
"i = 1d15;
attack( mob, victim, 6d6+10, \"left black claw\" );
attack( mob, victim, 6d6+10, \"right black claw\" );
if( random( 1, 8 ) == 1 ) {
  act_room( #tail, ch, obj, mob );
  attack( mob, victim, 5d5+10, \"barbed tail\" );
  }
if( random( 1, 9 ) == 7 ) {
  act_tochar( #bash, ch );
  act_notchar( #bashes, ch );
  interpret( mob, \"bash\" );
  }
if( i == 1 || i == 2 ) {
  act_notchar( #streamacid, mob );
  attack_acid( mob, victim, 7d9+12, \"stream of acid\" );
  }
"
