""
""
"stares down at you from atop the temple."
"silver-veined gargoyle of black marble"
""
""
"stare down at you from atop the temple."
"Carved out of the same midnight black stone as the temple, this foul beast
almost blends in with the walls.  This vile looking creature was once soley
built as a statue, but has somehow been animated for some unknown, dark deeds.
Wings jutting from its back, just barely poking up over its squared shoulders,
flap ever so slightly.  Crouched as it is, its impossible to tell its full
height, though the rippling muscles that appear evident beneath the stone...
or perhaps the stone itself, leads to the belief that this would be a
formidable foe.
"
"Soren"
""
"Hedrack"
"attack( mob, ch, 4d5+45, \"stone claw\" );
attack( mob, ch, 3d5+25, \"vicious claw swipe\" );
attack( mob, ch, 2d10+30, \"bite\" );
