"Standing fully as tall as a man at the shoulder, it is evident that this old
pack leader has seen a long and difficult life.  Less muscular than his young
brethren, he is leaner but much larger, and his thick, muscular neck and back
reveals that his bite is probably as terrible as younger wolves'.  This wolf's
coat is thicker and shaggier than a normal dog or wolf; it is bright white in
color everywhere except the tip of the tail, tips of the ears, the flanks, and
the muzzle, which have turned a peppered grey.  Frost rimes the air as this
grizzled old wolf exhales.  A single eye, pure white with a hint of faint
blue, watches the area warily, the other eye scarred over in a wicked slash of
tissue.
"
