"are here"
"A giant, night-black squid, perhaps stretching one hundred feet in length from
end to end.  The creature's torpedo-shaped body stretches nearly half the
length of the tentacles, and it lies on the ocean floor, near enough to the
stalagmite hot springs to not freeze to death, yet far enough away to remain
cool.  At one end of the body is a ridged tail, probably used for steering
under the water, while at the other, you can barely glimpse a jet-black,
razor-sharp beak.  The Deepmurk's eyes, nearly eighteen inches across, glimmer
a malevolent dirty gold, wide open even when the creature sleeps.
"
"Nereus"
