"snow"
"{snow cat} angarlish"
""
"feral"
"pads silently towards you, waiting to pounce."
"{snow cats} angarlishes"
""
"feral"
"move in a pack, questing for warmth."
"Glinting, ice-white eyes with sickly yellow pupils stand out from the rest of
the body of this legendary mountain predator.  Covered with strange matted
white fur, if this creature lay down on the icy tundra it would be
indistinguishable from a pile of dusty snow.  At first glance, the body shape
of this cat vaguely resembles a lion grown horribly bloated, standing roughly
the height of a troll at the shoulder.  Vastly more muscular than an ordinary
plains cat, the rear legs, jaws and neck are thick with corded muscle beneath
the heavy fur.  The creature's face is flattened more than a lion or other
cat's, and large, sabre-like canines protrude from both sides of its mouth. 
The ears are longer, but flatten against the creature's head, giving it an
almost horned appearance.  An anguished hunger is evident in this great snow
cat's eyes.
"
"Nereus"
""
"Nereus"
"attack( mob, victim, 8d6+35, \"raking claw\" );
attack( mob, victim, 8d6+35, \"raking claw\" );
if( attack( mob, victim, 14d16+90, \"saber-toothed bite\" ) ) {
  if( 1d25 == 5 && rflag( reset0, find_room( 29059 ) ) )
    acode( find_room( 29059 ), 1 );
  }
if( 1d6 == 1 ) {
  i = find_stat( mob, hit ) * 100;
  j = find_stat( mob, max_hit );
  if( ( i / j ) <= 35 ) {
    act_notchar( #howl, mob );
    if( !is_silenced( mob ) ) {
      act_area( #superhowl, mob );
      summon( mob );
      loop( all_in_room ) {
        if( is_player( rch ) || is_pet( rch ) ) {
          if( find_stat( ch, level ) < 30 && find_stat( ch, wis ) < 10 && 1d3 == 2 )
            interpret( ch, \"+flee\" );
          else
            do_spell( fear, mob, rch, 10 );
          }
        }
      }
    else {
      act_notchar( #canthowl, mob );
      }
    }
  }
"
E
"howl"
