chitinous shell is an unhealthy yellow green color with bright, scarlet
banding on ridges along its back.  Its legs are a greyish color with patches
of greenish mold eating away at its scarlet-tinged joints.  While the normal
moss beetle is a threat to mosses and lichens, preying upon them as its
natural food, this agitated beetle looks almost as if the moss is starting to
feed on it, enraging it and driving it to hostile acts.
