"ch"
"You ask $N for advice.
"
E
"advice1"
"Well, for starters, try to @btell@n an NPC @bhi@n by typing @bto <NPC> hi@n. 
They will often respond, giving you useful information or advice.  You can
also @bask@n them about things the same way you asked me about advice.
"
E
"introduce"
"You can also @bintroduce@n yourself to other players.  Before you introduce
yourself, people will only see your @bappearance@n and will not know your
name.  The command @bintroduce <target person>@n will introduce you to that
person if they understand the @blanguage@n you are currently speaking.  Right
now, you can only speak entish.  You will have to seek out trainers for other
languages in other cities.
"
E
"taverns"
"In your travels, particularly in other lands, you will probably come across
taverns.  The taverns of other cultures are often a good place to pick up
local information.  You can simply sit around and listen for the locals to
bring up interesting information or you can @btell@n the bartender @bhi@n to
see if they have any interesting information to offer you.
"
E
"advice2"
"That about covers the starting information I can offer you.  If you wish, I
can offer you further advice on the following things: @bents, weapons, spells,
practices,@n and @badventuring@n.  Simply @bask ent <topic>@n for advice on
that topic.
"
