"prac"
"You being your life knowing very little, however, you have the capacity to
learn.  Your ability to learn is measured in @bpractice@n points.  You can see
how many you have available by typing 'score'.  You use these practice points
to learn new skills and spells or to improve the ones you already know.
"
E
"prac2"
"There is no one single place to learn all the skills and spells you may be
able to learn.  The world is a large place and it is your job to seek out the
various beings who can teach you the skills you would like to learn. 
Fortunately, several of the locals here can teach you the basic skills you'll
need to survive.  The more advanced things you'll want to learn will require
you to seek out trainers on your own.
"
E
"prac3"
"To see if someone can teach you any spells or skills, simply type 'practice'. 
If someone is in the room who can train you, you will be shown a list of what
you can learn from them, how many pracitces it will cost to learn the skill,
and how many coppers the teacher will require to train you.  To practice a
skill type 'practice <skill name>'.
"
