great white shark with legs.  Its head is shaped like a crab's claw and
thickly plated.  The bulette peers out from narrow, yellow eyes with
blue-green pupils and brown-black sclera.  Protecting its body is a tough,
scaly shell which is a blue-green color that is almost sleek and reflective. 
Strong, stumpy legs that end in dull ivory nails support its tremendous
weight.  A long, scaly tail floats precariously from its hind portions, slowly
waving from side to side.
"
