wings replete with long, ebon feathers arc out behind him before folding back
down in a position of relaxed rest.  His skin, though white, retains a healthy
look to it and doesn't have the pallor of the grave about it.  His face,
framed by a halo of golden hair, is unlined and ageless.  Perhaps most
imposing of all, however, are his eyes.  Infinitely deep and without iris or
whites, his eyes are black as if no color has ever touched them and they seem
