"skeletal priest of death"
""
""
"watch you from the hollows where eyes should be."
"Human in form and size, the skeleton is nothing more than long-dried,
bleached-white bones.  Without muscle, sinew or cartilage, the bones somehow
retain their ability to stay connected in proper shape and form.  Muted clicks
and rasping rattles occur whenever this frightful figure moves as the bones
grate and shift against each other under the thic folds of a snowy-white robe
emblazoned with symbols holy to Morr, God of Death.  In one bony hand, this
skeleton holds a dessicated looking quill and, in the other, a
tattered-looking list of names, although the print is old and far too faded
for you to read.
"
"Talis"
""
"Talis"
