lean frame and a long, whipping tail.  From head to tail, it is covered in
rock-like scales, as thick as a shingle of slate on the shoulders, back, legs,
and arms, but flexible and supple along the joints.  An ebony-green, slime-
covered ridge of wicked-looking barbs runs the length of the creature's spine,
starting at the base of the neck and growing into lethal six inch barbs at the
tip of the tail.  The beast's powerful rear legs are complemented by slender,
muscular forelimbs, both tipped with six wicked, razor-sharp claws.  Slitted,
cat-like eyes gleam a cold, lifeless gold; a malevolent questing visible in
their gaze.  Beneath these glittering eyes of gold, a wide, ash-stained maw
waits, dozens of rows of triangular, black-stained teeth waiting to consume
