more that many begin to think he may even have already died.  While definite
signs of his age are upon him he is most certainly still in the realm of the
living as he watches you with curious eyes.  His glittering eyes are the most
lively thing about him these days, set in a face worn with lines of years and
toil.  He rests easily in his chair awaiting others to talk with.
