"stand in a group, clawed feet clacking on the stone."
"An abomination of pure evil, these bony humanoid skeletons resemble an
ordinary human corpse, stripped of its flesh - at first glance.  Small
aberrations from the norm make the creature much more disturbing: ordinary
hands have stretched into nine-inch points of needle-like bone; hollow eyes
follow your movements with a lifeless gaze.  Stranger still than an ordinary
corpse, some magic is visibly at work here, knitting bone into new shapes and
regenerating damage before your eyes.
"
"Nereus"
"Clerics with banishment have a chance to destroy the corpses and stop them from regenerating.
"
