"A bizarre amalgam of pointed ice crystals, it seems remarkable that this
creature is even alive, but as it blindly quests towards you - seeking warmth,
or life, or some other unknowable purpose - it is evidently intelligent.
Resembling a central, cylindrical pillar roughly the size of a wagon, six sets
of limbs jut out at angles spaced out around the body like spokes on a wheel.
The lower appendages are marginally thicker and appear to serve as legs: they
have two joints that both bend the same way, like the legs of a crab, allowing
for quite a bit of flexibility despite the fact that they are made of ice.
The upper appendages have an extra joint towards the very end, a crystalline
claw of sorts, that might allow the creature to manipulate objects or grasp
prey.  Nearly all of the creature is made of the same opaque, milk-white ice,
but in elongated crystals like one might see made of rock, an unusual
formation of ice.  The one exception to this is the creatures' upper
appendages, which are entirely translucent, pulsing bands of light fluctuating
within.  It is difficult to speculate on the habits of so alien a creature,
but it seems possible that the light is designed to stun the creatures of the
depths which are unused to light.
"
"Nereus"
""
"Nereus"
"i = 1d4;

// Attack with 2 legs
if( i == 1 ) {
  if( attack( mob, victim, 7d13+40, \"impaling leg\" ) || attack( mob, victim, 7d13+40, \"impaling leg\" ) ) {
    if( !victim )
      end;
    act_tochar( #impale, victim, null, mob );
    act_notchar( #impales, victim, null, mob );
    set_resting( victim );
    set_delay( victim, 32 );
  }
}

// Grab hold of someone and try to blind them
if( i == 2 ) {
  j = 0;
  k = 0;
  loop( j < 6 ) {
    if( attack( mob, victim, 4d10+22, \"grasping claw\" ) )
      k++;
    j++;
  }
  if( k >= 2 ) {
    act_tochar( #grasp, victim, null, mob );
    act_notchar( #grasped, victim, null, mob );
    j = 1d300;
    mind_message( victim, j, \"the stunning burst of light\" );
    inflict_mind( victim, mob, j, \"a stunning burst of light\" );
    if( victim && 1d6 == 2 )
      do_spell( blind, mob, victim, 20 );
  }
}

// Paralyze the room
if( i == 3 ) {
  act_notchar( #bright, mob );
  loop( all_in_room ) {
    if( rch != mob ) {
      if( !char_affected( rch, blind ) ) {
        if( 1d3 != 2 )
          do_spell( paralyze, mob, rch, 15 );
        else if( 1d2 == 2 )
          do_spell( confuse, mob, rch, 15 );
        else
          do_spell( slow, mob, rch, 15 );
      }
    }
  }
}

// Magic damage - mind blade with light
if( i == 4 ) {
  rch = rand_player( room );
  if( !char_affected( rch, blind ) ) {
    act_tochar( #ichooseyou, rch, null, mob );
    act_notchar( #hegotsmashed, rch, null, mob );
    j = 1d1000;
    mind_message( rch, j, \"the mind-crushing burst of light\" );
    inflict_mind( rch, mob, j, \"a mind-crushing burst of light\" );
    if( rch )
      set_delay( rch, 128 );
  }
}
"
