"story1"
"@B$N tells you:@n \"There is much unrest in our lands today.  The night winds speak
of treason in the near future.  Some of the men are unhappy with our lord, for
they fear he does not act.  Yet, perhaps I err, and they seek not change but
only encouragement.\"
"
E
"story2"
"\"No, the winds speak true,\"@B he continues.
"
E
"story3"
"\"It is assured,\"@B says he@n.  \"Ill fate shall soon fall upon our lord.  One of
our dearest shall bring it upon him, perhaps by sword.  Perhaps not.  Though I
wish also that our troubled people be avenged, so too must I admit that our
lord is in the right.  I regret to ask an outsider as you to intervene, yet
the others are treasoners, or would suspect me as one, should I ask them to
spy for me.\"
"
E
"story4"
"\"Be you willing to assist me and stay the hand of my lord's betrayer?\" @B$N
asks, pleading mercy of you with $S pained eyes@n.
"
