""
"stand very still, slings in hand."
"Covered in coarse, white, matted fur, this sleek humanoid male would probably
be difficult to see in the shadows of the cavern environment were it not for
the fact that bright-colored paints have been smeared across the entirety of
his body.  Enormous black eyes attest that this race has evolved underground
for what must have been thousands of years.  His mannerisms lend themselves to
staying well hidden, however -- his movements are fluid and no apparent rise
and fall of chest and shoulders with the intake of breath or other unnecessary
movement betrays the stillness needed to lurk in the shadow.  He wears no
clothing, but presumably the thick fur and layers of smeared paint serve as
both clothing and protection against the damn and cold of cavern life.
"
"Nereus"
