"Covered in reddish-brown hair,"
""
"forages in the understory."
"pygmy elephants"
"Covered in reddish-brown hair,"
""
"forage in the understory."
"Much smaller than a normal elephant, this creature is only about the size of a
warhorse.  Muscular haunches and shoulders taper down to surprisingly dainty
legs and feet, which pick about the undergrowth with ease.  Reddish-brown hair
covers its body in a thick layer everywhere except for its long trunk.  Two
yellowed tusks jut out straight from the mouth, looking very sharp.
"
"Kotoktok"
""
"Nereus"
"attack( mob, victim, 10d2+20, \"tusk pierce\" );
if ( attack( mob, victim, 5d7+18, \"trample\" ) ) {
  act_tochar( #trunk, victim, null, mob );
  act_notchar( #rtrunk, victim, null, mob );
  attack( mob, victim, 10d2+20, \"trunk squeeze\" );
}
attack( mob, victim, 3d4+18, \"trunk slap\" );
if (1d7 == 4) {
  act_notchar( #trumpet, mob );
  if (is_pet(mob)) {
    loop(all_in_room) {
if ( !is_player(rch) && !is_pet(rch)) {
        attack_sound(mob, rch, 3d5+20, \"intense trumpeting\");
      }
    }
  }
  else {
    loop(all_in_room) {
if ( is_player(rch) || is_pet(rch)) {
        attack_sound(mob, rch, 3d5+20, \"intense trumpeting\");
      }
    }
  }
}
