"This short and portly barkeep obviously takes care and pride in his
appearance.  His thick brown hair is gathered neatly at the nape of his neck
and is tied with a short black ribbon.  His clothes are worn, with tiny holes,
but have sense that this man, who is able to run a shop in such dire
surroundings, must know how to handle trouble.  been starched and pressed with
care.  He is wearing an oversized leather belt about his waist, held together
with a shiny, handmade brass buckle.  His breath smells faintly of ale, and
his eyes sparkle merrily as he bustles about the tavern.
"
"Talis"
