""
"j = get_quest( ch, 63 );
if( j < 6 ) {
  interpret( mob, #yet );
  interpret( mob, \"give musty.scroll\", ch );
}
if( i >= 7 ) {
  interpret( mob, #already );
  interpret( mob, \"give musty.scroll\", ch );
}
if( j == 6 ) {
  interpret( mob, #yay );
  set_quest( ch, 63, 7 );
  wait( 2 );
  if( !ch || !mob || is_fighting( mob ) )
    end;
  interpret( mob, #last );
  wait( 2 );
  if( !ch || !mob || is_fighting( mob ) )
    end;
  interpret( mob, #last2 );
}
"
E
"yet"
"say Hrm, how did you get this?  I never asked you to retrieve it.  I doubt the
authenticity of this scroll.  Here, take it.  I have no use for forgeries.
"
E
"already"
"say Why, you already brought me this scroll!  I don't believe there are two
copies in existence - this one may be a forgery.  Here, have it back.
"
E
"yay"
"say Fabulous!  I see that you have managed to retrieve the scroll without
resorting to violence!  Think on that, young one, there may come a time when
your brains will be more valuable to you than your brawn.
"
E
"last"
"say And now, young warrior, the last text I require from you is a treatise
written by the mighty Gyrael, one of the most skilled practitioners of
temporal magic ever to live.  Sadly, he was struck mad by a spell gone wrong,
and his brilliance was lost.  His last work was his greatest - and his rarest.
"
E
"last2"
"say One copy exists of the Treatise of Gyrael.  If you can retrieve it, I will
teach you what you seek.  I've heard that he wandered into the desert in his
madness, and was never seen again.  A sad end to a brilliant man.
"
!
